  "final_message": "**Status: reproduced, then fixed.** The bug is a regression in 3.5.14 and it is gone now.\n\n**Command**\n\n    npx vitest run --project unit packages/vue/__tests__/slotUnderscoreName.spec.ts packages/runtime-core/__tests__/componentSlots.spec.ts\n\n**Before the fix**\n- The reported case failed.\n  - Setup: `<BaseLayout>` has a `<template v-if=\"cond\" #randomslotname>` plus a sibling `<SubComponent>` with `#title` and `#_duration` templates.\n  - Result: `<div><p>cond</p><i>title works</i><span>default _duration</span></div>`. The `_duration` template was ignored and the fallback rendered.\n- The same markup without the `v-if` template rendered `<i>_duration works</i>`, so the trigger is the dynamic-slot sibling.\n- I ran the same markup against published Vue 3.5.13 and 3.5.14. 3.5.13 renders `_duration works` and 3.5.14 renders the fallback, which matches the report.\n\n**Cause**\n- In 3.5.14, `assignSlots` in `packages/runtime-core/src/componentSlots.ts` changed from `key !== '_'` to `!isInternalKey(key)`.\n- `isInternalKey` treats every key starting with `_` as internal, so compiled slot names like `_duration` were dropped.\n- This only happens when the child is mounted or patched without the optimized flag. That is the case inside a slot whose parent has dynamic slots, because `renderSlot` then emits a `BAIL` fragment.\n\n**Fix**\n- `assignSlots` now skips only the real compiler markers, `_` and `__`, through a new `isCompiledSlotsMarker` helper.\n- The stale-slot removal in `updateSlots` uses the same check. A `_`-prefixed slot behind a `v-if` is now removed when the condition turns false. That bug predates 3.5.14: 3.5.13 also left the slot in place.\n- I did not change `normalizeObjectSlots`. It still ignores `_`-prefixed keys in hand-written render-function slot objects. That is older than 3.5.14 and an existing test (`_inner`) expects it.\n\n**After the fix**\n- The reported case renders `<div><p>cond</p><i>title works</i><i>_duration works</i></div>`.\n- Slot content updates correctly when the parent re-renders, and the conditional `_`-prefixed template is removed again.\n- The full unit suite passes: 3378 passed, 5 skipped. `tsc`, eslint and prettier are clean.\n- I removed the fix to confirm the new tests fail without it (5 failures).\n\n**Files**\n- `packages/runtime-core/src/componentSlots.ts` (the fix)\n- `packages/runtime-core/__tests__/componentSlots.spec.ts` (two new tests)\n- `packages/vue/__tests__/slotUnderscoreName.spec.ts` (new, template-based tests including the reported case)\n",
  "run_command": "",
  "patch": "diff --git a/packages/runtime-core/__tests__/componentSlots.spec.ts b/packages/runtime-core/__tests__/componentSlots.spec.ts\nindex ad87e53..061eb5d 100644\n--- a/packages/runtime-core/__tests__/componentSlots.spec.ts\n+++ b/packages/runtime-core/__tests__/componentSlots.spec.ts\n@@ -43,6 +43,19 @@ describe('component: slots', () => {\n     expect(slots).toMatchObject({})\n   })\n \n+  test('initSlots: compiled slots whose name starts with an underscore should be kept when parent is using manual render function', () => {\n+    const slots = {\n+      foo: () => [h('span')],\n+      _foo: () => [h('i')],\n+      _: 1,\n+      __: [1],\n+    }\n+    const { slots: instanceSlots } = renderWithSlots(slots)\n+    // compiler markers are removed, slot names are not\n+    expect(Object.keys(instanceSlots)).toEqual(['foo', '_foo'])\n+    expect(instanceSlots).not.toHaveProperty('_')\n+  })\n+\n   test('initSlots: ensure compiler marker non-enumerable', () => {\n     const Comp = {\n       render() {\n@@ -162,6 +175,48 @@ describe('component: slots', () => {\n     expect(instance.slots).toHaveProperty('two')\n   })\n \n+  test('updateSlots: compiled slots whose name starts with an underscore should be updated and removed correctly', async () => {\n+    const flag1 = ref(true)\n+\n+    let instance: any\n+    const Child = () => {\n+      instance = getCurrentInstance()\n+      return 'child'\n+    }\n+\n+    const Comp = {\n+      setup() {\n+        return () => [\n+          h(\n+            Child,\n+            null,\n+            createSlots({ _: 2 as any }, [\n+              flag1.value\n+                ? {\n+                    name: '_one',\n+                    fn: () => [h('span')],\n+                  }\n+                : {\n+                    name: '_two',\n+                    fn: () => [h('div')],\n+                  },\n+            ]),\n+          ),\n+        ]\n+      },\n+    }\n+    render(h(Comp), nodeOps.createElement('div'))\n+\n+    expect(instance.slots).toHaveProperty('_one')\n+    expect(instance.slots).not.toHaveProperty('_two')\n+\n+    flag1.value = false\n+    await nextTick()\n+\n+    expect(instance.slots).not.toHaveProperty('_one')\n+    expect(instance.slots).toHaveProperty('_two')\n+  })\n+\n   test('updateSlots: instance.slots should be updated correctly (when slotType is null)', async () => {\n     const flag1 = ref(true)\n \ndiff --git a/packages/runtime-core/src/componentSlots.ts b/packages/runtime-core/src/componentSlots.ts\nindex 6114f6c..aff9ecd 100644\n--- a/packages/runtime-core/src/componentSlots.ts\n+++ b/packages/runtime-core/src/componentSlots.ts\n@@ -88,6 +88,14 @@ export type RawSlots = {\n \n const isInternalKey = (key: string) => key[0] === '_' || key === '$stable'\n \n+/**\n+ * Markers the compiler attaches to a compiled slots object (`_` for the slot\n+ * flag, `__` for the cache indexes). Unlike `isInternalKey`, this must only be\n+ * used for compiled slots, where every other key is a slot name, and a slot\n+ * name is allowed to start with an underscore (e.g. `<template #_foo>`).\n+ */\n+const isCompiledSlotsMarker = (key: string) => key === '_' || key === '__'\n+\n const normalizeSlotValue = (value: unknown): VNode[] =>\n   isArray(value)\n     ? value.map(normalizeVNode)\n@@ -180,7 +188,7 @@ const assignSlots = (\n     // when rendering the optimized slots by manually written render function,\n     // do not copy the `slots._` compiler flag so that `renderSlot` creates\n     // slot Fragment with BAIL patchFlag to force full updates\n-    if (optimized || !isInternalKey(key)) {\n+    if (optimized || !isCompiledSlotsMarker(key)) {\n       slots[key] = children[key]\n     }\n   }\n@@ -252,7 +260,10 @@ export const updateSlots = (\n   // delete stale slots\n   if (needDeletionCheck) {\n     for (const key in slots) {\n-      if (!isInternalKey(key) && deletionComparisonTarget[key] == null) {\n+      if (\n+        !isCompiledSlotsMarker(key) &&\n+        deletionComparisonTarget[key] == null\n+      ) {\n         delete slots[key]\n       }\n     }\ndiff --git a/packages/vue/__tests__/slotUnderscoreName.spec.ts b/packages/vue/__tests__/slotUnderscoreName.spec.ts\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..e3ac66c\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/packages/vue/__tests__/slotUnderscoreName.spec.ts\n@@ -0,0 +1,97 @@\n+import { createApp, nextTick, ref } from '../src'\n+\n+// Slot names that start with an underscore are valid slot names. They must\n+// not be mistaken for internal slot markers (`_`, `__`, `_ctx`, `$stable`).\n+describe('slot names starting with an underscore', () => {\n+  const BaseLayout = {\n+    template: `<div><slot name=\"randomslotname\"></slot><slot></slot></div>`,\n+  }\n+  const SubComponent = {\n+    template: `\n+      <slot name=\"title\"><span>default title</span></slot>\n+      <slot name=\"_duration\"><span>default _duration</span></slot>\n+    `,\n+  }\n+\n+  function mountApp(template: string, data: () => any = () => ({})) {\n+    const container = document.createElement('div')\n+    createApp({\n+      components: { BaseLayout, SubComponent },\n+      data: () => ({ cond: true, ...data() }),\n+      template,\n+    }).mount(container)\n+    return container\n+  }\n+\n+  it('sibling of a conditionally rendered slot template (reported case)', () => {\n+    const container = mountApp(`\n+      <BaseLayout>\n+        <template v-if=\"cond\" #randomslotname><p>cond</p></template>\n+        <SubComponent>\n+          <template #title><i>title works</i></template>\n+          <template #_duration><i>_duration works</i></template>\n+        </SubComponent>\n+      </BaseLayout>\n+    `)\n+    expect(container.innerHTML).toBe(\n+      `<div><p>cond</p><i>title works</i><i>_duration works</i></div>`,\n+    )\n+  })\n+\n+  it('control: without the conditional sibling', () => {\n+    const container = mountApp(`\n+      <BaseLayout>\n+        <SubComponent>\n+          <template #title><i>title works</i></template>\n+          <template #_duration><i>_duration works</i></template>\n+        </SubComponent>\n+      </BaseLayout>\n+    `)\n+    expect(container.innerHTML).toBe(\n+      `<div><i>title works</i><i>_duration works</i></div>`,\n+    )\n+  })\n+\n+  it('slot content is updated when the parent re-renders', async () => {\n+    const items = ref(['a', 'b'])\n+    const container = mountApp(\n+      `\n+      <BaseLayout>\n+        <template v-if=\"cond\" #randomslotname><p>cond</p></template>\n+        <SubComponent v-for=\"item in items\">\n+          <template #_duration><i>{{ item }}</i></template>\n+        </SubComponent>\n+      </BaseLayout>\n+    `,\n+      () => ({ items }),\n+    )\n+    expect(container.innerHTML).toBe(\n+      `<div><p>cond</p><span>default title</span><i>a</i><span>default title</span><i>b</i></div>`,\n+    )\n+    items.value = ['c', 'd']\n+    await nextTick()\n+    expect(container.innerHTML).toBe(\n+      `<div><p>cond</p><span>default title</span><i>c</i><span>default title</span><i>d</i></div>`,\n+    )\n+  })\n+\n+  it('conditionally rendered slot template is removed again', async () => {\n+    const show = ref(true)\n+    const container = mountApp(\n+      `\n+      <SubComponent>\n+        <template v-if=\"show\" #_duration><i>_duration works</i></template>\n+      </SubComponent>\n+    `,\n+      () => ({ show }),\n+    )\n+    expect(container.innerHTML).toBe(\n+      `<span>default title</span><i>_duration works</i>`,\n+    )\n+    show.value = false\n+    await nextTick()\n+    expect(container.innerHTML).toBe(\n+      `<span>default title</span><span>default _duration</span>`,\n+    )\n+  })\n+})\n"
